# Host-built artifacts — never copy these into the image. The CI job runs
# `dotnet build`/`dotnet test` directly on the runner *before* `docker build .`
# executes, so by the time Docker reads this context, every src/*/obj and
# src/*/bin already exists on disk. Without this exclusion, `COPY src/ src/`
# drags those host-platform build outputs into the image, where they conflict
# with the fresh `dotnet restore`/`publish` the Dockerfile itself performs.
**/bin/
**/obj/

.git/
.github/

apps/
docs/
tools/tracker/
sarvaghna/

**/node_modules/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
